# Day 3 – Deploy Strapi on AWS EC2 using Terraform

## Overview
On Day 3, the objective was to provision an AWS EC2 instance using **Terraform (Infrastructure as Code)** and deploy **Strapi** on the virtual machine, similar to the local setup done on Day 1.

This task focused on real-world cloud deployment challenges such as SSH access, key pair handling, Node.js setup, dependency installation, and system resource constraints.

---

## Tech Stack Used
- AWS EC2 (Ubuntu)
- Terraform
- Node.js & npm
- Strapi
- SSH
- Windows 11 (local machine)

---

## Infrastructure Provisioning (Terraform)

### Resources Created
- EC2 instance (Ubuntu)
- Security Group
  - SSH access (port 22)
  - Application access
- AWS Key Pair
- Public IP output

### Terraform Workflow Used
```bash
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply
terraform destroy


Terraform was used to automate the creation and destruction of infrastructure instead of manual EC2 setup.

SSH Access to EC2

Connected to the instance using SSH and a .pem key file

Correct OS user was used:

ubuntu for Ubuntu AMI

File permissions were fixed on Windows to allow SSH access

ssh -i day2-final.pem ubuntu@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>

Node.js & npm Setup

Faced conflicts due to older Node.js versions pre-installed on the VM

Removed broken dependencies and reinstalled Node.js

Final versions verified:

node -v
npm -v

Strapi Deployment on EC2
Steps Performed

Navigated to the Strapi project directory

Installed dependencies using npm

Ran Strapi in development mode

npm install
npx strapi develop

Issues Faced

npm installation freezes due to limited EC2 resources (t3.micro)

High CPU and memory usage observed

Network-related npm errors (ECONNRESET)

Strapi installation required retries

System monitoring was done using:

top
ps aux | grep node


These issues highlighted real-world limitations of small EC2 instances when running heavy Node.js applications.

Key Learnings

Terraform simplifies infrastructure management but requires correct state handling

AWS key pair name and local .pem file are different concepts

SSH access depends on:

Correct key pair

Correct OS user

Proper file permissions

Running Strapi on low-spec EC2 instances can cause performance issues

DevOps work involves significant troubleshooting and debugging

